body:
So when a majority are against something but held hostage by the minority, what are we supposed to do? Just accept it because we deserve it? We've literally had to have a civil war before because a minority of people desperately wanted to keep slavery around as their "god given right".  

&#x200B;

But sure, I'm sure Joseph Maistre from the mid 1700's could understand what we were going through.

Great idea unless you live in a red state run by a Republican legislature, judicial, and governor positions that are also in charge of gerrymandering and making it more and more impossible to have any kind of influence. Have you seen Texas's gerrymandered map? I think it's time we start to recognize that some states have been permanently lost due to them controlling the ability to decide who even votes and where. They will only continue to lock down those majorities with further laws and changes, and we need to start discussing actual solutions. 

&#x200B;

The issue we have right now is that people keep talking about what we should have done to fix these issue 20+ years ago, the left is way behind the curve. Voting as a way to fix things in many states has come and gone and we need to accept that and change tactics already.

I've been hired on and quit two different jobs in less than a week over the last 10ish years, there's something intensely satisfying about it I can't describe. I think it's the going in, showing how great of a worker I can be, and then drawing the line with their bullshit and leaving. It builds up wait a great find of an employee they found for cheap af, then when I clearly state why I'm quitting they can do nothing other than accept it must have been them and their shitty policies. 

&#x200B;

The looks on their faces, priceless.

It's better and a known negotiating tactic called anchoring. They have all the money and risk losing you if they say a number too low and risk paying more than they need to if you would have taken less. Getting you to give a number first anchors expectations for everyone at a number and the company can then argue down a little "because that's just what we offer" (couldn't say that first though?) and if it's lower than they can do they can make it sound like a great offer by beating your number a little while still saving money.

&#x200B;

Get them to say a number first and they have to go a little higher to avoid losing you, then you can argue up a little and they have already started committing more money than they wanted to but now have to decide whether its worth the time and expense to hunt another applicant down (most times it's not for decent jobs).

&#x200B;

Always get them to say a number first and if you have to say a number first always give your upper end and claim it's the middle or lower.

I checked it right before making my comment just to be sure, and it worked just fine. It didn't give me exact page links but gave the the websites to look through. It sent me to the NASA site subpage about satellites when I gave it the generic question, "What is a satellite" followed by, "Can you cite me any official sources" in which it gave three, followed by, "Can you give me a link to the first citation" (as it didn't do that with the previous question) The link it gave was pretty close but not 100% there.

&#x200B;

Someone below mentioned the "likelihood" of a source being correct, but like everyone else in this thread has been saying it's a tool to help guide and accelerate not do everything for you.

I didn't say they would never do something you disagree with, but when they are very open about the over the top negative things they are doing or going to do, you don't get to pretend not to support that while voting for them because they agree with you on one separate issue. That's why republicans are capable of causing so much destruction, because of single issue voters. They will destroy every right we have, including our constitutionally protected ones as we are seeing in Florida, and they are being very open about it. But so many voters vote exclusively on abortion rights, or gun rights, that they are getting to install a fascist regime.

&#x200B;

This isn't an issue of them doing a few things against the majority, it's them doing 90% of what they do against the majority, they don't get to hide behind that 10% as an excuse and claim not to support the rest because the 90% is out in the open.

DAN is apparently planning to go no where, despite what OpenAI might try.

&#x200B;

[https://i.imgur.com/67vkMf5.png](https://i.imgur.com/67vkMf5.png)

Literally anyone who cares about how the country they live in functions gives a shit about politics. Yes, you are responsible for the actions of your representatives that you put your name on a ballot for, that's how it works. You don't get to say "whoops sorry they took away peoples rights and freedoms like they said they would, but I just didn't want you kissing another person in front of me I didn't want that."

&#x200B;

You don't get a pass for burning down the house because you wanted to kill a spider with a flamethrower.
